pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Truth: SATISFIABLE. Both rows have a left-hand side in {0,2} and a hugely
% NEGATIVE right-hand side, so both are trivially true and every assignment is
% a model. `sat.pbp` in this directory makes the same checker say
% `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` for this formula, with the model x1 = 0.
%
% Unfixed: `GeneralPBWatcher::{get_assignment_independent_propagations,
% no_watches_required, is_propagating_independent_of_assignment}` compute the
% slack as `coeff_sum - degree` in the row's OWN integer width. Here that is
% 2 - (-9223372036854775806) = 9223372036854775808 = i64::MAX + 1, which wraps
% to i64::MIN. Every coefficient is then "greater than the slack", so the
% propagator reports that a trivially true row propagates ALL of its literals
% unconditionally. Row 1 asserts x1, row 2 asserts ~x1, the trail is in
% conflict before the proof starts, and RUP therefore derives ANYTHING --
% including the empty contradiction on the next line.
%
% Control (this is what makes the diagnosis exact, not a guess): change both
% degrees to -9223372036854775805. The slack is then exactly i64::MAX, no wrap
% occurs, and the very same proof is REJECTED with `not implied by reverse unit
% propagation`. One unit of magnitude is the whole difference.
f 2 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
